    "result_text": "The full suite is just the one acceptance test (the other two files are support classes), and it passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\n`membershipTier` now becomes `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create, falling back to the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules otherwise. Because the tier is a read-time derivation and the test asserts it via a `GET` after create, the household size is computed and persisted at create time \u2014 mirroring the existing `namesakeCount` idiom rather than adding new responsibilities to the mapper.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/CountHouseholdMembers.java`: after `AssignHouseholdId` has set the id and before `SaveOwner`, it iterates `ownerRepository.findAll()` counting owners with the same `householdId`, starting from `1` to include the new owner, and stores it via `owner.setHouseholdSize(...)`. Modeled directly on `CountNamesakes`.\n\n2. **Wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted `countHousehold` between `countNamesakes` and `flagBulkSignup`, keeping the `govern: [ transaction ]` governance consistent with its neighbours.\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 `model/Owner.java`: added the persisted `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, postgres, mysql), since `ddl-auto=none`.\n\n5. **Tier logic** \u2014 `mapper/OwnerMapper.java`: `membershipTier` now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, taking precedence over the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\nThe GOLD branch is the only new decision in the mapper; the counting logic lives in its own single-responsibility function class alongside the sibling count steps.",
